{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"uncanny-silvery-hawk","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nPure mutation plans still need to represent binding lifecycle decisions and prerequisite ordering without performing effects. Selection, filters, mode caps, and safety limits must exclude work before intents are eligible.\n\n## Outcome\nAdd versioned lifecycle intents and explicit inter-ticket dependencies to `TicketPlan`, and apply every global selection/limit before any lifecycle or remote effect.\n\n## Plan\n1. Model bind, confirm, re-key, retire, baseline, and comment-identity changes as versioned intents only.\n2. Encode create-before-link and parent-before-child prerequisites. A blocked prerequisite yields deferred disposition and emits no out-of-order mutation.\n3. Move selection, filter, mode cap, and global safety limit decisions into pre-effect planning.\n4. Cover tombstones, pending/index lag, moved keys, impossible links, partial snapshots, and filtered passes with ticket-sourced tables.\n\n## Testing\nPure tables assert exact intent/dependency/disposition values and poison repository/provider writes. Ordering tests vary each limit independently.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every named binding change is represented as a versioned lifecycle intent and performs no write during planning.\n- [ ] Create-before-link and parent-before-child prerequisites are explicit plan dependencies.\n- [ ] Blocked prerequisites produce deferred plans and no out-of-order mutation.\n- [ ] Selection, filter, mode cap, and global safety limits exclude work before any intent or remote effect is eligible.\n- [ ] Ticket-sourced tombstone, index-lag, move, link, partial-snapshot, and filtered cases have deterministic dispositions.\n\n## Out of scope\nPreview output and production coordinator execution.","id":"85f8-de1a-e425-4584","parent_id":"f828-6f5e-3b15-41f5","priority":1,"tags":["rp03","planner","tdd"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-03 S2 T2 — Plan lifecycle intents, dependencies, and pre-effect limits"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787028064503928001,"uuid":"7110ad24-0ef4-4605-aae4-49b8ca32ed4f"}